  "Id": 2248,
  "Title": "Taking charge to bring change",
  "NewsSubTitle": null,
  "NewsSummary": "Eight IED graduates qualify the competitive Federal Public Service Commission exams to get appointed as heads of government schools in Gilgit Baltistan.",
  "GlobalNews": false,
  "AlternateNewsTitle": null,
  "AlternateNewsSubtitle": null,
  "AlternateNewsSummary": null,
  "NewsContent": {
    "type": "doc",
    "content": [
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Eight IED graduates qualified the competitive Federal Public Service Commission exams to get appointed as heads of government schools in Gilgit Baltistan. Of 900+ applicants, our graduates were among the 28 candidates who qualified the competitive exams to take the school leadership roles. As leaders, they are determined to enable change and reform their schools. The outstanding performance of these graduates in the exams highlights the quality of IED's Master's programmes which prepare graduates to become catalysts for educational change. "
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "The graduates include:"
